('AS5712','AS5712','{\"key\": \"AS5712\", \"level\": 5712, \"title\": \"Mass Media and Popular Culture\", \"credits\": 4, \"courseCode\": \"AS5712\", \"labBearing\": false, \"description\": \"This senior seminar focuses on the relation between mass media and different forms of popular culture and explores different theoretical approaches to the understanding of media in modern society. The course examines how popular media communicate ideas about the world, about identity, and our sense of self. Reading across television, film, music, art, and the popular press, the course considers relationships between the mass media, institutions, identity, relations of power, and historical, economic, social, and political contexts.\", \"liberalArts\": false, \"departmentId\": 10, \"upperDivision\": true, \"catalogVersion\": \"2026-2027\", \"classifications\": []}','{\"type\": \"review-required\", \"reason\": \"unsupported prerequisite prose\", \"sourceText\": \"( Undergraduate Level AS 2112 Minimum Grade of D- or Undergraduate Level AS 2112 Minimum Grade of TD- or\\nUndergraduate Level AS 2122 Minimum Grade of D- or Undergraduate Level AS 2122 Minimum Grade of TD- or\\nUndergraduate Level AS 2252 Minimum Grade of D- or Undergraduate Level AS 2252 Minimum Grade of TD- or\\nUndergraduate Level AS 2262 Minimum Grade of D- or Undergraduate Level AS 2262 Minimum Grade of TD- or\\nUndergraduate Level AS 2263 Minimum Grade of D- or Undergraduate Level AS 2263 Minimum Grade of TD- or\\nUndergraduate Level AS 2300 Minimum Grade of D- or Undergraduate Level AS 2300 Minimum Grade of TD- or\\nUndergraduate Level AS 2640 Minimum Grade of D- or Undergraduate Level AS 2640 Minimum Grade of TD- or\\nUndergraduate Level AS 3215 Minimum Grade of D-\\n\\nor Undergraduate Level AS 3215 Minimum Grade of TD- or Undergraduate Level AS 3222 Minimum Grade of D- or\\nUndergraduate Level AS 3222 Minimum Grade of TD- or Undergraduate Level AS 3270 Minimum Grade of D- or\\nUndergraduate Level AS 3270 Minim